    "title": "Where to watch the Miami Heat vs. Charlotte Hornets NBA play-in game for free tonight",
    "text": "Miami Heat guard Norman Powell (24) shoots against Charlotte Hornets guard Kon Knueppel during the first half of an NBA basketball game, Tuesday, March 17, 2026, in Charlotte, N.C.(AP Photo/Nell Redmond)If you purchase a product through a link on our site, we may receive compensation.By Jenna Malinowski | JMalinowski@mlive.comThe Miami Heat and the Charlotte Hornets will face off tonight as the NBA playoffs officially begin.Fans can catch the play-in game exclusively on Amazon Prime Video at 7:30 p.m. ET. New subscribers can start with a 30-day free trial.The Heat earned the No. 10 seed after finishing the season with a 43-39 record, while the Hornets are the No. 9 seed with a 44-38 record. The winner of tonight’s game will advance to play the loser of the No. 8 Orlando Magic and the No. 7 Philadelphia 76ers for the right to the No. 8 seed and to play the Detroit Pistons in the first round of the playoffs. The loser of tonight’s game will officially be eliminated from the playoffs. The Heat vs. Hornets game will serve as the first playoff matchup tonight. The Portland Trail Blazers and the Phoenix Suns will face off at 10 p.m. ET, also on Amazon Prime Video. NBA PLAY-IN TOURNAMENTNo. 10 Miami Heat vs. No. 9 Charlotte HornetsWhen: Tuesday, April 14, 2026Where: Spectrum Center, Charlotte, NCTime: 7:30 p.m. ETStreaming: Amazon Prime Video2026 Michigan high school girls soccer: MHSAA schedule and where to watch2026 Michigan high school lacrosse: MHSAA schedule and where to watchDetroit Pistons fans can still score playoff tickets for tonight’s Game 2 for under $60Jenna is a sports commerce writer for MLive.com. She writes about how to stream and get ticket deals for your favorite sporting events and where you can find gear for the Detroit Tigers, the Detroit Red Wings,...",
